# The build context is the repository root and most of it is not the site: five
# of the six client libraries, their build outputs, and the toolchains that
# produced them. Sending those is a slow build and a fat cache key on every
# commit that touches a Rust test.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.svelte-kit
**/.svelte-kit
build
**/build
dist
**/dist
target
**/target
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.egg-info
.venv
bin
obj
.gradle
.DS_Store
# `tools/` and `openapi.json` are copied by name, and `apps/docs` is the site.
# The libraries are not in this image's graph at all — except the one manifest
# the lockfile makes it name, which is copied explicitly.
packages/python
packages/rust
packages/kotlin
packages/csharp
packages/cpp
